{
 "$id": "lynkomni/chart-of-accounts.v2",
 "description": "One global chart of accounts in the core (Step 0, blueprint 42 A). The double-entry journal is a projection of the event log at every tier: tiers decide which reports are shown, never what is recorded. A country that requires its own chart gets it as a country-pack mapping (`chart_of_accounts` in the pack: global code to the local code and name); the global codes are what every service, export and test use. Shared by every language, like the other contract files. Version 2 (OFFICE UPDATE, blueprint 66, section 4 step D1) keeps every version 1 code and posting unchanged and adds the accounts LynkAcc needs for bills, assets, loans, advances, held-back tax, group balances, funds and exchange rates. Each account has a `group` for the statements (cash, current_asset, non_current_asset, current_liability, non_current_liability, equity, income, other_income, cost_of_sales, expense); `contra` marks an account that grows against its type (loss of value so far); `intercompany` marks the balances removed in group books.",
